{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5398",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a potential modulator of NCI-H650 through a series of interconnected targets. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N exerts its effects by targeting multiple proteins that are also targets of palmarumycin CP18, a compound that in turn influences NCI-H650. Specifically, Mollicellin N is shown to interact with A704, Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, and P2X purinoceptor 1, all of which are involved in pathways that may ultimately affect NCI-H650. The shared target of palmarumycin CP18 across these pathways implies a possible mechanism of action involving the modulation of cellular processes that are critical for NCI-H650 function. The cumulative evidence supports a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and NCI-H650, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
